### [the sump floor](sump_cache)
---
Relic: cipher
Point: 900, -2300, 1400
Roles: cipher_treasure
Item: relay_salvage
Qty: 3
Hidden: yes
Scene: cipher_sump_look
Scan: Relay salvage, dropped when the builders stripped this place and never picked up.
---
`Hidden:` keeps it off the crew's list of places until somebody has BEEN down here, which
is the reward for taking the spill instead of cutting the throat. A party that cut their
way in never learns this room had anything in it.

It is still on the web - a route may pass straight through the sump - so it is a thing to
notice rather than a thing to unlock.

### [the spare rod](rod_place)
---
Relic: cipher
Point: 1900, -300, 2600
Roles: cipher_clue
Item: clue_rod
Starts when: reach cipher_coil 1000
---
A spare keying rod, racked where a technician would want it. It is cut for a housing this
size - and there is more than one housing this size.

### [the real throat](at_throat)
---
Relic: cipher
Point: -1200, -600, 800
Roles: cipher_throat
Hidden: yes
Scene: cipher_throat_look
Scan: The throat drops under the false mouth and bends away. A fall of shielding is jammed across the short way on.
---
HIDDEN until somebody finds the way out of the false mouth (science or helm, in
`cipher_false_look`). Hidden is a property of the LIST: a crew that stumbles down here
on the way somewhere else has found it anyway.

