## [Dialogue](dialogue)

What the Cipher's places say. See the Voice's file for how a place scene works.

### [The Dead End](cipher_false_look)
---
Backdrop: pic:cv_wall_a
---
% The false mouth is a smooth bubble with one way out, and the way out is the way you came in. The murk is thick enough to lean on. Somebody built this room to be given up on.

- [Sweep the walls for a seam](cipher_false_seam) if science ; check science 7 else cipher_false_smooth, reveal at_throat, signal cipher_throat_found
- [Feel for a draught in the murk](cipher_false_draught) if helm ; check helm 8 else cipher_false_still, reveal at_throat, signal cipher_throat_found
- [Call Storm](cipher_false_storm)
- [Give up on it]()

### [A Seam](cipher_false_seam)
---
Backdrop: pic:cv_wall_a
---
% Low on the floor, behind a lip of shielding, the wall is not a wall: a throat, angled back under the way you came. The real way in.

- [Take it]()

### [A Draught](cipher_false_draught)
---
Backdrop: pic:cv_wall_a
---
% The murk is moving - slowly, but moving - down and back, towards the floor behind you. Something below is open.

- [Follow it]()

### [Smooth](cipher_false_smooth)
---
Backdrop: pic:cv_wall_a
---
% Smooth, all the way round. Whoever finished these walls finished them well.

- [Look again](cipher_false_look)
- [Leave it]()

### [Still](cipher_false_still)
---
Backdrop: pic:cv_wall_a
---
% The murk hangs dead still round the suit. Or the suit is not still enough to tell.

- [Try again](cipher_false_look)
- [Leave it]()

### [Storm, on the Dead End](cipher_false_storm)
---
Speaker: prof_storm
---
% A dead end in a relay? No. Relays do not have dead ends, they have DECOYS. The builders hid this once in a nebula and once again inside itself - look for the second hiding place, and look low.

- [Understood](cipher_false_look)

### [The Real Throat](cipher_throat_look)
---
Backdrop: pic:cv_rubble
---
% The throat drops under the false mouth and bends away. A little way on, a fall of the relay's own shielding is jammed across the short way into the coil. There is a longer way down, if you would rather not cut.

- [Work the fall loose](cipher_fall_free) if engineering ; check engineering 10 else cipher_fall_stuck, open throat_fall
- [Cut it with the beam](cipher_fall_cut)
- [Take the long way](cipher_fall_long)

### [Loose](cipher_fall_free)
---
Backdrop: pic:cv_rubble
---
% The plate shifts, grinds, and slides away into the murk. The short way is open.

- [On]()

### [Jammed](cipher_fall_stuck)
---
Backdrop: pic:cv_rubble
---
