### [The Long Way](cipher_fall_long)
---
Backdrop: pic:cv_rubble
---
% The spill drops out of the throat before the fall and comes up under the sump - longer, darker, and nobody has been down it in a thousand years. Anything down there has been waiting.

- [Understood]()

### [The Coil](cipher_coil_look)
---
Backdrop: pic:cv_wall_b
---
% The coil is the relay's body: a round room with its dead core hanging in the middle and a thousand years of sediment on everything below it. The sediment is heaped wrong - as if something underneath had been pushing up through it.

- [Read the sediment](cipher_coil_sediment) if science ; check science 8 else cipher_coil_mud, reveal sump_cache, signal cipher_sump_read
- [Listen to the core](cipher_coil_listen) if comms ; check comms 8 else cipher_coil_dead, signal cipher_core_heard
- [Move on]()

### [Hollow Underneath](cipher_coil_sediment)
---
Backdrop: pic:cv_wall_b
---
% Hollow underneath. There is a room below this one that the murk has been hiding, and something in it is heavier than silt.

- [Mark it]()

### [Mud](cipher_coil_mud)
---
Backdrop: pic:cv_wall_b
---
% Mud, a thousand years deep. It is not telling you anything today.

- [Try again](cipher_coil_look)
- [Move on]()

### [A Tick](cipher_coil_listen)
---
Backdrop: pic:cv_wall_b
---
% The core is dead, but its housing still rings when something further in does - a tick, very faint, very regular. Whatever keys this relay is still keeping time.

- [Log it]()

### [Silence](cipher_coil_dead)
---
Backdrop: pic:cv_wall_b
---
% Silence, and the sound of your own suit.

- [Listen again](cipher_coil_look)
- [Move on]()

### [The Sump Floor](cipher_sump_look)
---
Backdrop: pic:cv_rubble
---
% Relay salvage, under a thousand years of murk - dropped when the builders were stripping this place and never picked up again.

- [Ask Eddy](cipher_sump_eddy) if comms
- [Haul it later]()

### [Eddy, on Relay Windings](cipher_sump_eddy)
---
Speaker: crazy_eddy
---
% Relay core windings? Nobody has seen relay windings since my grandmother's day. What do you mean, you do not know what they are worth? I am TELLING you what they are worth!

- [We'll see]()

### [The Keying Chamber](cipher_keying_look)
---
Backdrop: pic:cv_obelisk
---
% The keying chamber has the only hard floor in the relay, and in the housing at the far end the Cipher sits in its notches, ticking. A rack beside it holds one spare rod.

- [Match the rod to the housing](cipher_keying_match) if engineering ; check engineering 7 else cipher_keying_wrong, signal cipher_rod_matched
- [Read the notching](cipher_keying_read) if science ; check science 8 else cipher_keying_blank
- [Call Storm](cipher_keying_storm)
- [Get to work]()

### [A Second Housing](cipher_keying_match)
---
Backdrop: pic:cv_obelisk
---
% The spare rod slides into a notch that is not the Cipher's. There is a second housing cut into the floor, and it is empty. This rod was made for another relay.

- [Tell Vex](cipher_keying_vex)

### [Vex, on the Rod](cipher_keying_vex)
---
Speaker: chief_vex
---
% Vex. Two housings, one rod, one Cipher. So there were two of these relays - or somebody meant there to be. Bring the rod home. Storm will want to know where its twin went.

- [Will do]()

### [It Will Not Seat](cipher_keying_wrong)
---
Backdrop: pic:cv_obelisk
---
% The rod will not seat in any notch you try. Not yet.

- [Try again](cipher_keying_look)
- [Leave it]()

### [A Count](cipher_keying_read)
---
Backdrop: pic:cv_obelisk
---
% The notching is a count, not a key: every notch a day this relay kept time. The last one was cut a thousand years ago, and the tick has gone on counting with nobody to cut the next.

- [Move on]()

### [Notches](cipher_keying_blank)
---
Backdrop: pic:cv_obelisk
---
% Notches, and more notches. The pattern is there. You are not seeing it.

- [Look again](cipher_keying_look)
- [Move on]()

### [Storm, at the Housing](cipher_keying_storm)
---
Speaker: prof_storm
---
% The Cipher. Still keeping time - of course it is. Scan it, tether it, and bring the spare rod too. I have a feeling it opens something we have not found yet.

- [Understood]()

